data/
__pycache__/
# No trailing slash: in a forest worktree `web/node_modules` is a SYMLINK to the
# main checkout, and a `node_modules/` pattern matches directories only, so git
# would otherwise offer to commit an absolute-path symlink.
node_modules
*.pyc
.env
# Same live secrets as .env — the launcher writes one of these beside it
# whenever it backs up an existing .env before overwriting it.
.env.backup-*
.aether/debug/runs/*
# The canonical CV is personal data. It lives on the shared data volume
# (data/canonical_cv.pdf, registered via `python -m truth.answers <path>`),
# never in git history. Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored
# `assets/` would match at any depth and swallow the built frontend bundle
# in api/static/assets/.
/assets/
# The operator's own screening answers and job-search queue. Both are personal
# data (phone, address, salary band, target companies) and both have a tracked
# `.example` counterpart that documents the shape without carrying anyone's
# details. Anchored so they only ever match at the repo root.
/answers.local.yaml
/agent/targets.md